# Use `lib/widgets` Custom Components

Always prefer project widgets from `lib/widgets/` over raw Flutter widgets when a match exists.

Import via:

```dart
import 'package:flutter_task/widgets/widgets.dart';
```

## Widget map

| Use case | Widget |
|---|---|
| Text / labels | `CustomText` |
| Buttons / CTAs | `CustomButton` |
| Loading | `CustomLoader` |
| Tappable styled box | `CustomContainer` |
| Standard app bar | `CustomAppBar` |
| Collapsible / hero header | `CustomSliverAppBar` |
| Scrollable sliver screens | `SliverScaffold` |
| Text input | `CustomTextField` |
| Search input | `CustomSearchField` |
| OTP / PIN input | `CustomPinCodeTextField` |
| Network image | `CustomNetworkImage` |
| Avatar | `CustomImageAvatar` |
| Dialog | `CustomDialog` |
| Empty state | `EmptyDataWidget` |
| Step progress | `StepProgressBar` |
| Paginated list footer | `PaginationLoaderSliver` |

## Rules

- Do **not** use raw `Text`, `ElevatedButton`, `TextField`, `AppBar`, `CircularProgressIndicator`, etc. when a custom widget covers the same need.
- Use `SliverScaffold` + `CustomSliverAppBar` for scrollable screens with a header/hero area.
- Only use raw Flutter widgets when no custom widget fits, or for low-level layout (`Row`, `Column`, `SizedBox`, `Padding`).

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 16))
ElevatedButton(onPressed: () {}, child: Text('Save'))

// ✅ GOOD
CustomText(text: 'Hello', fontSize: 16.sp)
CustomButton(label: 'Save', onPressed: () {})
```
